_Simple Robot_ is a `Java` application that lets you see a robotic arm following a ball. It works by performing [gradient descent](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gradient_descent) on a cost function. This cost function is defined as follows:
Let $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ be the position of a ball, $\boldsymbol{\theta} \in \mathbb{R}^4$ be the robot's degrees of freedom (joint angles), and $\text{DK}(\boldsymbol{\theta}) \rightarrow  \mathbf{y} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ be a function that receives $\boldsymbol{\theta}$ and outputs $\mathbf{y}$, the end position of the robot arm tip ($\text{DK}$ is usually called the [direct kinematics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forward_kinematics) function). Finally, the cost function is:
$$\min_{\boldsymbol{\theta}} |\text{DK}(\boldsymbol{\theta}) - \mathbf{x}|^2$$
$$\text{s.t} \;\;\; C_i(\boldsymbol{\theta}) > 0, \forall i \in \{1,\dots, k \}$$

Here, $C_i$ are functions that constrain the degrees of freedom, *e.g.*: $\theta_1 > 0 \text{ and } \theta_1 < 2 \pi$.

Feel free to download the program below.
                
![*Simple Robot* app video](https://youtu.be/rb4BLRtzkJ8)

